{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774709,"nonce":"lsUz8YZLtmooaKMAhgfrA0rJ7bw=","title":"k8s log tail → log pipeline (ADR-0013)","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #6 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `feat/adr-0013-k8s-log-tail` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-14T15:43:21Z · Merged: 2026-07-14T15:52:59Z\n\n\nWires the missing **log source** for the log pipeline (ADR-0013). The pipeline (`LogService`: chunk → gzip → object store + Postgres offset index → live SSE tail + secret redaction) was built and tested, but nothing in production ever called `LogService::append` — only tests pushed bytes in. The module even said so.\n\nThis adds the source: the control-plane executor tails each running Pod's stdout via the k8s API log endpoint (`Api::\u003cPod\u003e::log_stream`, `follow: true`) and pumps the chunks into the pipeline, keyed by the `{run, step, attempt}` fence. It's the **agentless, control-plane-pull** model — a separate channel from results (results ride the acked egress sidecar, ADR-0042; logs are best-effort, so a dropped tail never fails the run).\n\n\n- **engine** — new `Executor::log_stream(\u0026StepRun) -\u003e Option\u003cBox\u003cdyn LogChunks\u003e\u003e` port method (default `Ok(None)`, same idiom as `output`/`results`) plus the `LogChunks` trait. Takes the fenced `StepRun`, not an `ExecHandle`, so the source derives from the fence with no handle bookkeeping. Engine stays dependency-free (no `futures`).\n- **k8s executor** — implements `log_stream` via `Api::\u003cPod\u003e::log_stream(follow, container=\"step\")`; `PodLogChunks` reads it in 8 KiB bites. Hoisted the `\"step\"` container name into a `STEP_CONTAINER` const shared with `build_pod`/`container_exit_code`.\n- **server** — `log_tail.rs`: `pump_log_stream` (pure drain loop) + `LogTailer` (per-fence dedup, spawns tasks, re-arms after an early failure such as a still-Pending Pod).\n- **converged driver** — `tick_once`/`spawn_driver` take an optional `LogService` and ensure a best-effort tail for every `Running` step each tick; `main` passes `Some(logs)`.\n- **fix (adjacent)** — `SecretInjectingExecutor` forwarded `output` but **not** `results`, so it silently dropped ADR-0041 named results on any secrets-wired deployment. Now forwards both `results` and `log_stream`.\n- **infra** — `.workspaces/` (git worktrees for parallel agents) is gitignored.\n\n\n- Hermetic unit tests (no cluster): pump drains in order, redacts registered secrets, skips empty chunks; `LogTailer` dedups per fence (via a gated fake executor).\n- Live k8s tail test (`log_stream_tails_pod_stdout`) is `#[ignore]`d + `SCARAB_TEST_KUBE`-gated, same as the egress sidecar's live test.\n- Full workspace green, clippy clean.\n\n\nThe live k8s path still isn't exercised in CI (needs the dev kind cluster — same gate as the egress sidecar's live test).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}